WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Literal bells.

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.713
- There we go.

00:00:01.713 --> 00:00:02.688
(bells jingling)

00:00:02.688 --> 00:00:03.728
- There we go.

00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:05.288
Christmas (bleep).

00:00:05.288 --> 00:00:07.955
(holiday music)

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:14.339
- [Selorm] Christmas music, in my opinion,

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:16.139
is one of the most interesting genres.

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:18.473
Chances are, you're listening
to Christmas classics

00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:20.423
that were made decades ago.

00:00:20.423 --> 00:00:22.321
In fact, the two most
modern songs that you'll

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.361
probably find on Billboard's
top Christmas list

00:00:24.361 --> 00:00:26.703
are "All I Want For Christmas Is You"

00:00:26.703 --> 00:00:29.100
by Mariah Carey, and
"Last Christmas" by Wham!

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.751
Many artists don't even bother to write

00:00:30.751 --> 00:00:33.340
original Christmas songs
knowing they can make a killing

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.559
singing the same classics
that everyone already knows.

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:36.980
So I thought, what's the harm in trying

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.980
and while fiddling around with my ukulele,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.647
I came up with this:

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.399
I had a feeling that I was on to something

00:01:05.399 --> 00:01:07.407
so I asked my college friend Irene

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:08.937
to co-write the song with me.

00:01:08.937 --> 00:01:10.097
- My name is Irene.

00:01:10.097 --> 00:01:11.675
Despite my musical
background, I don't feel

00:01:11.675 --> 00:01:14.337
all too confident in writing music.

00:01:14.337 --> 00:01:16.406
I'm more of a singer and piano player.

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:19.065
- I love songwriting but
I feel like I've never

00:01:19.065 --> 00:01:20.566
tried to challenge myself.

00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:22.492
But it would be really cool
to try something different

00:01:22.492 --> 00:01:23.413
like a Christmas song.

00:01:23.413 --> 00:01:24.433
- [Selorm Voiceover] Even
though Irene and I had

00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:25.962
a lot of musical talent,
we needed some help

00:01:25.962 --> 00:01:27.578
when it came to writing the song.

00:01:27.578 --> 00:01:29.245
So we sought out advice from

00:01:29.245 --> 00:01:31.719
hit singer and songwriter Scotty Grand.

00:01:31.719 --> 00:01:33.498
- Christmas songs are really about

00:01:33.498 --> 00:01:35.126
painting pictures with their lyrics.

00:01:35.126 --> 00:01:36.559
When it comes to finding a great concept,

00:01:36.559 --> 00:01:38.565
go with things that are universal:

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.658
love, getting your heart broken,

00:01:40.658 --> 00:01:42.458
but you still have to stand out.

00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:43.938
What haven't you heard them talk about?

00:01:43.938 --> 00:01:47.624
Go there and then bring it
home with something human.

00:01:47.624 --> 00:01:49.108
- Even though I like a
lot of Christmas songs,

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.491
I don't always relate to them.

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:52.040
- I've never had a
white Christmas, either.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.540
So any song that involves snowing,

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.339
I can't relate to it, sorry.

00:01:55.339 --> 00:01:57.101
- That's so sad, Irene.

00:01:57.101 --> 00:01:59.102
- Well, I'm from Guam, it's hot there.

00:01:59.102 --> 00:02:00.710
- Let's definitely go with that theme.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.869
Like just an unconventional Christmas.

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:04.489
- Songs should be simple.

00:02:04.489 --> 00:02:07.772
It could be repetitive, just
like Mariah Carey's song.

00:02:07.772 --> 00:02:08.748
She uses repetition.

00:02:08.748 --> 00:02:11.308
- For the chorus that I
have so far, it's like

00:02:11.308 --> 00:02:13.697
♪ Doesn't matter where you are ♪

00:02:13.697 --> 00:02:17.617
♪ When it plays you're
right where you belong ♪

00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:19.639
♪ This whole world is a gift we're given ♪

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:22.466
♪ So put a little Christmas in it ♪

00:02:22.466 --> 00:02:24.748
♪ Ooh, put a little Christmas in it ♪

00:02:24.748 --> 00:02:27.658
♪ Ooh, put a little Christmas in it ♪

00:02:27.658 --> 00:02:29.830
- Hit Christmas songs,
they use seventh chords.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.190
They use diminished chords.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:34.148
One, three, five, that's a regular chord.

00:02:34.148 --> 00:02:37.910
Now if you go two steps down,
that's the seventh chord.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.755
And these chords kind of play
off the jazz era of music.

00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:43.588
Where the lyrics were
telling more of a story.

00:02:54.198 --> 00:02:55.031
- Dude.

00:02:55.031 --> 00:02:56.180
I did it, I made words (laughing)

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.751
- You made words.

00:02:57.751 --> 00:03:01.918
♪ Tryna find that Christmas cheer ♪

00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:11.583
- Yeah, Christmas mood was the word.

00:03:13.608 --> 00:03:14.867
- I did something bad.

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:16.576
I got so excited about me and Irene

00:03:16.576 --> 00:03:19.048
making some progress on the song

00:03:19.048 --> 00:03:20.677
that I actually sent an email out

00:03:20.677 --> 00:03:23.667
to our entire office
saying that we'd perform it

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:24.836
and the only day that we could

00:03:24.836 --> 00:03:26.427
do that is three days away.

00:03:26.427 --> 00:03:27.706
I'm a little worried because more than

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:29.205
half of the song isn't done yet.

00:03:29.205 --> 00:03:30.776
Right now, I'm actually talking to a

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.525
friend of mine, RJ Tolson.

00:03:32.525 --> 00:03:35.228
He's a great music maker, he's going to

00:03:35.228 --> 00:03:37.386
make us a track that we can perform live.

00:03:37.386 --> 00:03:39.609
So I woke Irene up.

00:03:39.609 --> 00:03:42.609
So I wrote something for the chorus.

00:04:01.926 --> 00:04:03.426
What do you think?

00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:06.053
We're doing it, bitch.

00:04:06.053 --> 00:04:06.886
We're doing it.

00:04:06.886 --> 00:04:08.493
- I need to go back to sleep.

00:04:08.493 --> 00:04:10.448
- Okay, I love you.

00:04:10.448 --> 00:04:11.940
Bye.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.869
We are stuck up here in this little loft.

00:04:13.869 --> 00:04:16.160
We've got some of the lyrics down so far.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.799
We just have to write the second verse

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:20.600
and we're pretty much good.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.521
Right, Irene?

00:04:21.521 --> 00:04:22.951
- And then practice it a million times.

00:04:22.951 --> 00:04:24.645
- So this is how many lines we're probably

00:04:24.645 --> 00:04:25.687
going to need for it.

00:04:25.687 --> 00:04:28.791
♪ So you something something something ♪

00:04:28.791 --> 00:04:30.691
(marker squeaking)

00:04:30.691 --> 00:04:31.524
So basically--

00:04:31.524 --> 00:04:32.357
- [Irene] That's a lot of lines.

00:04:32.357 --> 00:04:33.746
- [Selorm] This is how
many spots we need to fill

00:04:33.746 --> 00:04:36.079
before we get to the chorus.

00:04:36.964 --> 00:04:38.719
- First two needs to be more about

00:04:38.719 --> 00:04:42.802
the things you do to get
in the Christmas spirit.

00:04:47.176 --> 00:04:49.825
- So I wrote, it won't
matter where you are,

00:04:49.825 --> 00:04:52.158
whether home is near or far.

00:04:56.432 --> 00:04:58.640
♪ ether home is near or far ♪

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.473
♪ All it takes is just a memory ♪

00:04:59.473 --> 00:05:02.973
♪ Of a time when you were ♪

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.093
- We just need two more lines.

00:05:10.093 --> 00:05:12.282
- No, we need to stop
using the word "feel".

00:05:12.282 --> 00:05:13.522
- We don't use it that much.

00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:14.423
- Yeah, we do.

00:05:14.423 --> 00:05:16.733
♪ Time when you were young ♪

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:18.554
♪ And you hold your-- ♪

00:05:18.554 --> 00:05:23.263
♪ And you hold it close and don't let go ♪

00:05:23.263 --> 00:05:24.303
- What are you going to do

00:05:24.303 --> 00:05:27.012
to get yourself back to this
place when you were young?

00:05:27.012 --> 00:05:28.865
You're going to play your
motherfucking favorite

00:05:28.865 --> 00:05:30.155
Christmas song.

00:05:30.155 --> 00:05:31.803
But I don't know how to get there.

00:05:31.803 --> 00:05:32.636
- Yeah.

00:05:49.724 --> 00:05:52.349
♪ Your favorite Christmas song ♪

00:05:52.349 --> 00:05:53.766
- That's perfect.

00:05:56.056 --> 00:05:56.889
Fuck yeah.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:57.722
- Yes.

00:05:57.722 --> 00:05:59.106
We got it, we got it.

00:05:59.106 --> 00:06:00.056
- Yes.

00:06:00.056 --> 00:06:01.881
You think we're going to do okay?

00:06:01.881 --> 00:06:03.248
- We'll see.

00:06:03.248 --> 00:06:06.427
The next main thing is
just not being nervous

00:06:06.427 --> 00:06:08.888
and performing it with confidence.

00:06:08.888 --> 00:06:09.758
- I'm going to be sad if they don't

00:06:09.758 --> 00:06:11.727
like the song or if they don't feel it.

00:06:11.727 --> 00:06:14.283
Who gives a shit what
they think? (laughing)

00:06:14.283 --> 00:06:15.116
We made a great song, so whatever, right?

00:06:15.116 --> 00:06:18.116
(audience cheering)

00:09:39.134 --> 00:09:41.384
(applause)

00:09:44.034 --> 00:09:45.374
- That was incredible.

00:09:45.374 --> 00:09:46.762
- I identified with the song greatly

00:09:46.762 --> 00:09:48.251
because none of my family lives

00:09:48.251 --> 00:09:50.473
in California, they all
live in the midwest.

00:09:50.473 --> 00:09:53.531
- Okay, I thought this was
like a Jason Mraz song.

00:09:53.531 --> 00:09:55.051
- Even if you don't celebrate Christmas,

00:09:55.051 --> 00:09:56.961
you kind of celebrate
the season and the vibe.

00:09:56.961 --> 00:09:59.273
I like that tagline of
"put some Christmas in it",

00:09:59.273 --> 00:10:00.931
so put some Christmas in it.

00:10:00.931 --> 00:10:03.193
- This was about making new traditions

00:10:03.193 --> 00:10:05.411
and new memories and I think the song

00:10:05.411 --> 00:10:06.831
showcases that a lot.

00:10:06.831 --> 00:10:08.073
- When is it coming out on iTunes

00:10:08.073 --> 00:10:10.673
because I'll buy it legally (laughs).

00:10:10.673 --> 00:10:11.891
- When we started writing this

00:10:11.891 --> 00:10:13.931
I didn't really know if we could do it.

00:10:13.931 --> 00:10:15.201
But then to actually perform it

00:10:15.201 --> 00:10:17.611
in front of people was mindblowing.

00:10:17.611 --> 00:10:19.131
- This was an original song that

00:10:19.131 --> 00:10:20.753
no one had ever heard her before.

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.051
When you're writing an original,

00:10:22.051 --> 00:10:24.609
it's putting puzzle pieces
together, but you don't know

00:10:24.609 --> 00:10:26.262
what the puzzle is supposed to look like.

00:10:26.262 --> 00:10:29.451
I think because we really
believed in what we were writing,

00:10:29.451 --> 00:10:30.950
we were able to make
something really special.

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.801
This really shows you that whatever

00:10:32.801 --> 00:10:35.803
artistically you feel
like, you want to express

00:10:35.803 --> 00:10:37.307
Or do, you can do it.

00:10:37.307 --> 00:10:40.045
You could write the next "All
I What For Christmas is You."

00:10:40.045 --> 00:10:42.205
It's still a challenge,
but you'll be surprised

00:10:42.205 --> 00:10:44.594
at what you're actually capable of doing

00:10:44.594 --> 00:10:46.387
once you set your mind to something.

00:10:46.387 --> 00:10:50.286
- (speaking together) Merry Christmas.

00:10:50.286 --> 00:10:51.119
(laughing)

00:10:51.119 --> 00:10:53.452
- That was in tune, we were both in unison

00:10:53.452 --> 00:10:55.278
- It was a harmony.

00:10:55.278 --> 00:10:59.278
♪ Put a little Christmas in it. ♪

